00:13:05,994 --> 00:13:11,291
And yet I also knew, even then, what
a powerful anesthetic vulgarity could be.

251
00:13:12,542 --> 00:13:16,421
I told myself I was only going
to chronicle the decadence,

252
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:20,800
an excuse I'd return to many
times in my career as a writer.

253
00:13:22,135 --> 00:13:26,055
Susan's dad was the West Side's
pediatrician to the stars,

254
00:13:27,098 --> 00:13:31,728
treating their progeny from everything
from anorexia nervosa to zits.

255
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:37,400
Fashionably, Dr. Reynolds didn't
accept new patients or insurance.

256
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:39,152
[Susan] Hey, Bret.

257
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:41,320
I didn't think you'd come.

258
00:13:41,404 --> 00:13:44,198
Yes! Thank God Bret's here.
Now it's a party.

259
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:48,828
Well, I wasn't going to, but I figured
it would be useful for my novel.

260
00:13:49,454 --> 00:13:50,496
Screenplay.

261
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,749
-You're writing a screenplay?
-[inhales, exhales deeply]

262
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:55,626
-Well, that's a relief. Someone has to.
-[chuckles]

263
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:58,087
-[Bret] Where are your parents?
-Palm Springs.

264
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,464
[Bret] So, they're out of town?

265
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:02,550
Oh, don't worry, Al and Linda
arranged for me to babysit.

266
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,093
Al and Linda?

267
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:06,012
-[Susan] Aspen.
-Hey.

268
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,305
I'm gonna get a drink.

269
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:09,557
You can go right through those doors.

270
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:12,685
Yeah, I know that.
I've been coming here since I was 12.

271
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:17,273
I've been coming to Farrah Fawcett
since I was 12.

272
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:22,403
♪ Seemed like the real thing
Only to find ♪

273
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:25,406
♪ Mucho mistrust
Love's gone behind… ♪

274
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:32,789
[Bret] Senior year was when we started
throwing parties like rich adults.

275
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:37,960
We spent our parents' money
on the best champagne,

276
00:14:38,044 --> 00:14:40,713
the purest coke, and top-shelf liquor.

277
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:46,469
We put out their Lalique glass bowls
and filled them with our cigarettes.

278
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:52,016
These were the gilded weapons we used to
fend off the stifling world of childhood.

279
00:14:54,769 --> 00:14:58,439
We were all just doing impressions
of the kind of people we wanted to be.

280
00:14:59,107 --> 00:15:01,275
Until it stopped being an impression.

281
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:06,072
Hi.

282
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:08,157
-[whooping]
-[chattering]

283
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:09,742
[♪ "Heart of Glass" continues]

284
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:33,266
Gin martini with a twist, please.

285
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:36,894
Is that such a good idea?
You know you're not supposed to drink.

286
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:38,813
Of course.

287
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:40,648
Why don't you take this one?

288
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,192
Thanks.

289
00:15:43,276 --> 00:15:45,278
[chattering, laughing continues]

290
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:51,868
♪ Once I had a love and it was a gas ♪

291
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,035
[Susan] You want this?

292
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,581
Hey, Susan, can I talk to you?

293
00:15:57,999 --> 00:16:01,002
♪ Seemed like the real thing
Only to find... ♪

294
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:03,504
You need permission
to talk to your boyfriend?

295
00:16:03,588 --> 00:16:04,839
Relax, Thom.

296
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,636
Excuse us.

297
00:16:18,603 --> 00:16:19,896
You're all over him.

298
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:21,314
What? Who?

299
00:16:23,441 --> 00:16:25,234
Do you think I'm stupid?

300
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:30,031
Susie Q.

301
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:33,075
[chuckling] I am so proud of this girl.

302
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:35,119
I mean, look how pretty she is.

303
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,205
Remember fat camp?

304
00:16:37,288 --> 00:16:38,998
-Thom, do you know the story?
-Uh-huh.

305
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:40,374
I had just turned ten.

306
00:16:40,458 --> 00:16:42,960
Liz shipped me off to a fat farm in Tahoe,

307
00:16:43,044 --> 00:16:45,963
told me she'd give me a thousand dollars
for every pound I lost,

308
00:16:46,047 --> 00:16:47,506
and that's where I met Susan.

309
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:50,218
-She wasn't even fat.
-I was maintaining.

310
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:53,137
You are gonna be
the first female president.

311
00:16:53,221 --> 00:16:54,764
You know that, right?

312
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:56,015
Thanks, Deb.

313
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:58,100
[♪ "Square Biz" playing]

314
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:02,104
What the hell is Cha Cha
doing north of the 10?

315
00:17:02,188 --> 00:17:05,733
♪ Flashback
Who's that dancing to the latest? ♪

316
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:08,027
♪ Suave, debon, the greatest… ♪

317
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:10,655
-She showed up with some juniors.
-Slut.

318
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:13,658
-We've got to kick her out.
-Sorry?

319
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,202
She's my nemesis.

320
00:17:16,911 --> 00:17:18,913
-Thought Cornelia Guest was your nemesis.
-Thought your mom was your nemesis.

321
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:21,582
-Stay out of this, Thom.
-I can't just kick her out, Debbie.

322
00:17:22,083 --> 00:17:23,084
I can.

323
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,544
Don't cause a scene.
This is Robert's party.

324
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:29,173
[scoffs] No, this is our party
we're throwing for Robert.

325
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,884
Why are his feelings
more important than mine?

326
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:34,804
-They're not. You're being a child.
-I'm actually not.

327
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:37,098
If someone you hated
showed up to this party,

328
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:40,685
I would physically remove them,
and I think you know that.

329
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:43,854
Just once I wish you could be
that friend for me.

330
00:17:43,938 --> 00:17:47,650
♪ So shy, oh my
Had to change that real quick ♪

331
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:51,654
♪ Had to use a few tricks
You know, like my femme fatale ♪

332
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:53,531
I'll see you at Dance Off!, Cha Cha.

333
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:56,742
Better hurry back to Compton.
I wouldn't want your pole to get cold.

334
00:18:10,298 --> 00:18:12,258
[♪ "Square Biz" continues]

335
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:17,138
Hi, baby.

336
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:19,640
I'm so happy you came.

337
00:18:20,391 --> 00:18:21,767
I'm not.

338
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:26,105
I mean, I am, but for observing,
not for partying.

339
00:18:27,481 --> 00:18:29,525
-I have something for you.
-I'm not really in the--

340
00:18:29,609 --> 00:18:31,068
No, it's a gift.

341
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:44,165
I know how much you like books.

342
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:45,916
It's a first edition.

343
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:49,962
This came out last month.
They're all first editions.

344
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:54,550
Sorry, that was…

345
00:18:56,469 --> 00:18:57,637
Thank you.

346
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:04,310
Listen, why don't you go find Susan?
I'll catch up with you later.

347
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,939
[♪ tense music playing]

348
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:13,444
Debbie, I'm…

349
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:19,700
[Debbie sniffling]

350
00:19:49,689 --> 00:19:52,066
-[chattering, music playing in distance]
-[Debbie] Get out.

351
00:19:53,234 --> 00:19:54,276
Go.

352
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:57,947
[sighs]

353
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:04,995
[Ryan] Hey, Debbie.

354
00:20:05,663 --> 00:20:08,499
-Hey.
-Wh… What are you doing in here all alone?

355
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:10,918
[chuckles softly]

356
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:17,258
[sighs]

357
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:21,554
[Ryan] Everything okay, like, at home?

358
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,724
Yeah, it's just Bret.

359
00:20:25,516 --> 00:20:28,227
He ignores me. He's always reading.

360
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:30,020
-Reading what?
-I don't know, books.

361
00:20:30,104 --> 00:20:31,814
-That's messed up.
-Yeah.

362
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:34,650
So, I went and I bought him one
and he didn't even appreciate it.

363
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:37,945
It sounds like he doesn't appreciate you.

364
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:40,531
[Debbie] I'm 18, and I'm an LA ten.

365
00:20:41,115 --> 00:20:43,701
I shouldn't have to beg
my boyfriend to touch me.

366
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:48,456
If you were my girlfriend,
you wouldn't have to beg me for anything.

367
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:51,208
No?

368
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,260
You'd be the one begging me.

369
00:21:06,557 --> 00:21:08,768
[partygoer 1] Dude, I'm telling…
That's what I'm saying.

370
00:21:08,851 --> 00:21:11,103
-[partygoer 2] That's like your thing.
-[partygoer 1] I know, I know.

371
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:14,148
Give me a chance, I gotta get in there.
I got to work my magic a little.

372
00:21:14,899 --> 00:21:18,319
They're the most beautiful girls I've seen
in my entire life. Of course, I would--

373
00:21:18,402 --> 00:21:20,279
[partygoer 2] Well, I mean,
how many can you handle at one time?

374
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:21,822
Come on, man.

375
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:25,284
-I couldn't do more than two or three…
-[laughs]

376
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:26,368
Who, uh…

377
00:21:27,495 --> 00:21:28,662
You guys know Susan?

378
00:21:28,746 --> 00:21:31,499
That's whose house this is,
the girl throwing the party?

379
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:34,168
I thought this was Robert's party.

380
00:21:35,795 --> 00:21:37,004
It is.

381
00:21:38,255 --> 00:21:39,465
We go to Brentwood.

382
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:40,883
-I'm Rohmer.
-Bret.

383
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:43,552
So, you're Robert's friends?

384
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:45,721
Kinda.

385
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:49,183
-What do you mean kinda?
-I don't know.

386
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:52,228
Well, I mean, we went to middle school
with the guy back in Chicago.

387
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:54,605
Ran into each other
at the Galleria last week,

388
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:56,357
and he said we should stop by.

389
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,858
I haven't seen him in years though.

390
00:21:57,942 --> 00:22:02,279
For sure I thought he'd be in, like,
jail by now. [laughs]

391
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:05,950
What's that supposed to mean?

392
00:22:06,951 --> 00:22:09,453
-I mean, you know Robert.
-Actually, I don't.

393
00:22:09,537 --> 00:22:10,996
[♪ tense music playing]

394
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:12,540
Why would he be in jail?

395
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:18,087
He… He wouldn't.
He was cleared of any wrongdoing.

396
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:22,925
It was a dumb joke about his mom
after she fell down the stairs.

397
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:26,637
A bunch of people assumed
maybe Robert, like…

398
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,182
killed her.

399
00:22:36,230 --> 00:22:38,232
-[chattering, laughter]
-[♪ soft rock song playing]

400
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:49,159
Who are you looking for?

401
00:22:51,287 --> 00:22:52,538
No one.

402
00:22:52,621 --> 00:22:53,622
[♪ song ends]

403
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:55,708
[♪ "The Weakness in Me" playing]

404
00:22:59,587 --> 00:23:00,921
I love this song.

405
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:07,970
♪ I'm not the sort of person who falls ♪

406
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:12,766
♪ In and quickly out of love ♪

407
00:23:12,850 --> 00:23:17,104
♪ But to you I gave my affection ♪

408
00:23:17,187 --> 00:23:19,523
♪ Right from the start ♪

409
00:23:22,151 --> 00:23:26,322
♪ I have a lover who loves me ♪

410
00:23:27,448 --> 00:23:31,785
♪ How could I break such a heart? ♪

411
00:23:31,869 --> 00:23:35,789
♪ Yet still you gained my attention… ♪

412
00:23:39,710 --> 00:23:41,837
Remember the first time we danced?

413
00:23:43,714 --> 00:23:47,217
-Of course.
-The freshmen luau at Trader Vic's.

414
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:50,721
That was the first time we held hands too.

415
00:23:51,889 --> 00:23:53,766
I love that you remember all that stuff.

416
00:23:56,143 --> 00:23:59,480
My fingers felt so tiny next to yours.

417
00:24:02,441 --> 00:24:04,610
Remember I recited that poem?

418
00:24:06,737 --> 00:24:12,284
"Nobody, not even the rain,
has such small hands."

419
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:15,329
E.E. Cummings.

420
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,706
[Thom] Yeah, I remember.

421
00:24:19,917 --> 00:24:21,335
Remember how drunk we got?

422
00:24:25,506 --> 00:24:27,257
"Beer before liquor, never sicker."

423
00:24:30,386 --> 00:24:32,388
That's the poem you should have recited.

424
00:24:32,471 --> 00:24:34,473
[♪ melancholy music playing]

425
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:42,106
[sniffles softly]

426
00:24:46,902 --> 00:24:48,904
[♪ pensive music playing]

427
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:51,281
[no audible dialogue]

428
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:28,694
[♪ "Presence of a Man" plays]

429
00:25:36,744 --> 00:25:38,704
[♪ "Funkytown" playing]

430
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:41,915
-[cheering]
-"Funkytown." Funk, yeah.

431
00:25:48,255 --> 00:25:52,885
♪ Gotta make a move
To a town that's right for me ♪

432
00:25:55,763 --> 00:26:00,392
♪ Town to keep me movin'
Keep me groovin' with some energy ♪

433
00:26:00,476 --> 00:26:02,478
[cheering, whooping]

434
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:08,525
♪ Well, I talk about it, talk about it
Talk about it, talk about it ♪

435
00:26:08,609 --> 00:26:12,321
-Hey, it's a party, not a one-man show.
-Yeah, Thom, it is a party…

436
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:16,325
♪ Talk about, talk about
Talk about movin' ♪

437
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:18,911
His party.

438
00:26:26,627 --> 00:26:28,629
[♪ "Funkytown" continues in distance]

439
00:26:30,255 --> 00:26:32,508
[both moaning]

440
00:26:35,719 --> 00:26:37,721
[both breathing heavily]

441
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:40,557
Oh, my God. You're such a good person.

442
00:26:40,641 --> 00:26:41,934
No, I'm not.

443
00:26:48,357 --> 00:26:50,359
[♪ eerie music playing over "Funkytown"]

444
00:26:58,826 --> 00:27:00,744
[♪ "Funkytown" continues]

445
00:27:02,454 --> 00:27:04,456
[cheering, whooping]

446
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:17,803
I really need to talk to you about Robert.

447
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:18,929
Does he seem okay to you?

448
00:27:19,847 --> 00:27:21,598
[Bret] No, Susan, he doesn't.

449
00:27:21,682 --> 00:27:24,935
He's a pathological liar
who spent time in a mental institution.

450
00:27:25,018 --> 00:27:28,355
Robert does not seem okay. I've been
trying to tell you guys that for weeks.

451
00:27:28,438 --> 00:27:30,566
Bret, this isn't about you, okay?

452
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:32,985
He's not really supposed to drink
on his medication.

453
00:27:33,068 --> 00:27:34,903
[Bret] His medication? Jesus, Susan.

454
00:27:35,529 --> 00:27:37,698
-What the fuck?
-He's a disturbed individual.

455
00:27:37,781 --> 00:27:38,782
He's dangerous.

456
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:42,786
[♪ "Funkytown" continues in distance]

457
00:27:58,427 --> 00:28:00,637
Uh, Ryan.

458
00:28:04,099 --> 00:28:05,225
Ryan, stop. I can't.

459
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:07,477
You… You can't what?

460
00:28:08,604 --> 00:28:11,064
Uh, sleep with you.

461
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,358
You're too big.

462
00:28:14,776 --> 00:28:17,237
It's… It's not always this big.
It's just when I'm hard.

463
00:28:17,321 --> 00:28:19,072
-Yeah. Mm-hmm.
-You know?

464
00:28:19,156 --> 00:28:20,407
Can we talk about it?

465
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:23,076
I don't know if talking's gonna help.

466
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:25,412
Okay.

467
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:28,373
Okay.

468
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:30,667
We don't have to do anything.

469
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:34,588
I just like being around you.

470
00:28:38,216 --> 00:28:39,927
I really do think you're a good person.

471
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:43,221
-[floorboard creaking]
-[footsteps approaching]

472
00:28:43,305 --> 00:28:45,307
[♪ eerie music playing]

473
00:28:49,227 --> 00:28:50,646
[whispers] Is someone in here?

474
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:52,731
[Ryan] Hello?

475
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:06,036
♪ Won't you take me to
Funkytown? ♪

476
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:07,162
What did you say to him?

477
00:29:08,038 --> 00:29:09,790
-When?
-Five minutes ago.

478
00:29:09,873 --> 00:29:11,375
I saw you whisper something to him,

479
00:29:11,458 --> 00:29:14,795
and then he pounded a handle of vodka
and started going insane.

480
00:29:14,878 --> 00:29:16,046
[Bret] He's always been insane,

481
00:29:16,129 --> 00:29:19,383
because he's an actual
institutionalized lunatic.

482
00:29:19,466 --> 00:29:22,844
He's psycho, and he kidnapped Matt,
and he kidnapped Rhonda,

483
00:29:22,928 --> 00:29:25,722
-and I think he might have pushed his mo--
-Oh, my God, Bret, listen to yourself.

484
00:29:25,806 --> 00:29:26,807
You're the psycho.

485
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:28,892
[♪ "We Got the Beat" playing]

486
00:29:30,143 --> 00:29:31,228
[crowd gasps]

487
00:29:35,273 --> 00:29:36,274
[gasping]

488
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:40,529
Do something.

489
00:29:41,363 --> 00:29:42,489
I am doing something.

490
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:47,828
-Bearing witness is doing something.
-Oh, my God!

491
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:51,456
Thom! Thom! Has anyone seen Thom?

492
00:29:51,540 --> 00:29:54,251
-[♪ song continues in distance]
-[floorboard creaking]

493
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:05,137
[♪ eerie music playing]

494
00:30:06,346 --> 00:30:07,764
What the fuck, dude?

495
00:30:08,598 --> 00:30:10,726
Let me guess,
you're one of Cha Cha's friends?

496
00:30:12,936 --> 00:30:14,187
You can't be in here.

497
00:30:23,530 --> 00:30:25,949
Oh, my God, Ryan.
He has a… He has a knife.

498
00:30:26,825 --> 00:30:29,119
Listen, you didn't know we were in here.

499
00:30:29,202 --> 00:30:30,370
-Yeah.
-It's fine.

500
00:30:31,288 --> 00:30:32,706
Just leave us alone.

501
00:30:40,338 --> 00:30:42,591
-Oh, my God.
-Thank you.

502
00:30:43,967 --> 00:30:44,968
It's fine.

503
00:30:45,761 --> 00:30:46,762
[Debbie] Ryan.

504
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:57,355
[♪ song continues]

505
00:30:57,439 --> 00:30:58,899
♪ We got the beat ♪

506
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:01,943
♪ We got the beat… ♪

507
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:03,987
-Thom. Where were you?
-Nowhere.

508
00:31:04,071 --> 00:31:06,531
-I don't know.
-Something's seriously wrong with Robert.

509
00:31:08,408 --> 00:31:10,160
It's his party.
You said he can do whatever he wants.

510
00:31:10,243 --> 00:31:13,205
-Thom, please, help me. Please. Please.
-Fine.

511
00:31:13,914 --> 00:31:15,707
Hey, man. Let's go inside.

512
00:31:16,333 --> 00:31:17,793
[crowd gasping]

513
00:31:19,669 --> 00:31:20,670
Stop!

514
00:31:21,505 --> 00:31:23,381
What are you doing? [grunting]

515
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:28,136
Stop it.

516
00:31:35,727 --> 00:31:37,938
[Thom] What the hell, dude? Get off of me.

517
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:41,233
-[Thom] What the fuck?
-Are you okay?

518
00:31:41,316 --> 00:31:42,943
I'm fine, I'm fine, I'm fine!

519
00:31:44,653 --> 00:31:47,030
-♪ We got the beat ♪
-♪ We got the beat ♪

520
00:31:47,781 --> 00:31:50,033
-♪ We got the beat ♪
-♪ We got the beat ♪

521
00:31:50,951 --> 00:31:53,120
-♪ We got the beat ♪
-♪ We got the beat ♪

522
00:31:53,203 --> 00:31:54,830
-♪ We got the beat ♪
-♪ We got the beat ♪

523
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:57,874
-♪ We got the beat, we got the beat ♪
-♪ We got the beat ♪

524
00:31:57,958 --> 00:31:59,042
[♪ song ends]

525
00:31:59,126 --> 00:32:00,293
[♪ tense music playing]

526
00:32:00,377 --> 00:32:01,753
Why are you crying?

527
00:32:04,172 --> 00:32:06,508
[sniffles]

528
00:32:07,342 --> 00:32:08,343
Uh…

529
00:32:09,094 --> 00:32:10,303
Do… Do you want money?

530
00:32:10,387 --> 00:32:11,680
I know where the safe is.

531
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:14,391
Are you an actor? My dad is a producer.

532
00:32:14,474 --> 00:32:16,101
He will put you in one of his movies.

533
00:32:20,021 --> 00:32:21,565
Look, just let her go.

534
00:32:21,648 --> 00:32:23,233
Let her go, and I'll stay.

535
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:34,578
[partygoers murmuring]

536
00:32:50,594 --> 00:32:52,596
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

537
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:01,563
He's not moving.

538
00:33:02,147 --> 00:33:03,315
Why isn't he moving?

539
00:33:10,071 --> 00:33:11,156
Thom, are you gonna help him?

540
00:33:11,239 --> 00:33:12,782
I'm done helping that guy.

541
00:33:16,620 --> 00:33:18,205
Hey, what are you doing?

542
00:33:43,104 --> 00:33:44,814
[♪ music fades out]

543
00:33:44,898 --> 00:33:47,234
[♪ tense music plays]

544
00:34:10,757 --> 00:34:12,759
[Robert gasping]

545
00:34:14,094 --> 00:34:15,679
[applause[

546
00:34:17,722 --> 00:34:19,849
-Are you okay?
-Only when you're around.

547
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:29,818
-[Susan] Thom, Thom.
-[partygoers gasp]

548
00:34:29,901 --> 00:34:31,945
-Hey, Thom. Cool it, man.
-[Susan] Bret.

549
00:34:40,578 --> 00:34:42,998
-[thudding]
-[partygoers gasp]

550
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:46,793
-[screaming in distance]
-[partygoer] What the fuck?

551
00:34:46,876 --> 00:34:47,877
Debbie.

552
00:34:48,837 --> 00:34:50,755
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

553
00:34:50,839 --> 00:34:52,173
[screaming continues]

554
00:35:06,896 --> 00:35:08,857
-[Bret] Debbie!
-[Debbie] Help!

555
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:11,109
[Bret] Debbie, Debbie, it's locked!

556
00:35:11,192 --> 00:35:12,193
[Ryan] He's got a knife!

557
00:35:12,277 --> 00:35:13,987
Open the door, or we'll kick it down!

558
00:35:14,070 --> 00:35:15,989
Hey, whoever you are, open up!

559
00:35:17,157 --> 00:35:18,158
[door unlocks]

560
00:35:18,241 --> 00:35:19,492
[♪ music ends]

561
00:35:22,704 --> 00:35:24,623
[♪ tense music plays]

562
00:35:42,557 --> 00:35:45,393
-[crying]
-Hey, Deb. Hey, hey. Are you okay?

563
00:35:45,477 --> 00:35:46,770
-Who's in here?
-[Debbie sniffles]

564
00:35:47,395 --> 00:35:51,399
[Ryan] He won't say anything.
He just stands there with a knife.

565
00:35:53,568 --> 00:35:54,653
What kind of knife?

566
00:35:54,736 --> 00:35:57,322
[door creaks]

567
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:03,870
Jesus.

568
00:36:19,219 --> 00:36:21,179
I think it's time you leave.

569
00:36:22,013 --> 00:36:23,181
Don't you?

570
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:33,441
Thom, watch out.

571
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:43,827
-Is that what you want?
-Yeah.

572
00:36:46,287 --> 00:36:47,497
That's what I want.

573
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:50,834
Well, then that's what I want.

574
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:54,963
Goodbye, Thom.

575
00:37:06,599 --> 00:37:07,684
Oh, my God.

576
00:37:07,767 --> 00:37:09,769
[crying] Oh, my God,
I thought we were gonna die.

577
00:37:10,729 --> 00:37:13,398
-You're okay. You're okay.
-[cries]

578
00:37:16,860 --> 00:37:18,445
[Debbie sniffles]

579
00:37:30,206 --> 00:37:31,708
[TV plays, indistinct]

580
00:37:34,419 --> 00:37:36,546
[TV news anchor]
…here's a brief look at our weather.

581
00:37:36,629 --> 00:37:40,300
Fair temperatures are predicted
for the downtown civic center tomorrow…

582
00:37:40,383 --> 00:37:42,302
[TV fades, continues indistinctly]

583
00:37:55,565 --> 00:37:59,110
[Debbie sighs deeply] Such a headache.

584
00:38:00,653 --> 00:38:03,072
I cannot be hungover or dehydrated
for Dance Off!

585
00:38:03,156 --> 00:38:05,408
We should have just canceled this party.

586
00:38:05,492 --> 00:38:06,493
Yeah.

587
00:38:07,368 --> 00:38:10,205
I would stab someone
for a drink right now. [chuckles]

588
00:38:11,831 --> 00:38:13,833
It's a joke. I'm funny.

589
00:38:14,751 --> 00:38:16,419
I keep trying to tell you guys that.

590
00:38:16,503 --> 00:38:18,505
[vacuum cleaner whirring]

591
00:38:22,717 --> 00:38:25,094
No mas vacuum, por favor.

592
00:38:25,178 --> 00:38:26,179
[vacuum cleaner stops]

593
00:38:26,262 --> 00:38:27,555
Gracias.

594
00:38:27,639 --> 00:38:28,723
[Bret] I'm still confused.

595
00:38:29,641 --> 00:38:31,768
What were you and Ryan doing
in Susan's bedroom

596
00:38:31,851 --> 00:38:33,394
-without your shirts on?
-[Debbie scoffs]

597
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:35,355
Fucking.

598
00:38:36,940 --> 00:38:40,610
No, the guy, the creep,
he made us take them off.

599
00:38:43,196 --> 00:38:44,864
How'd you know that guy, anyway?

600
00:38:47,909 --> 00:38:48,952
I didn't.

601
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:51,412
Never seen him before.

602
00:38:51,496 --> 00:38:52,997
He said your name, though.

603
00:38:53,540 --> 00:38:54,624
[Thom] I don't think so.

604
00:38:55,792 --> 00:38:57,001
He definitely did, Thom.

605
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:00,672
Maybe he heard you and Debbie say it.

606
00:39:05,552 --> 00:39:06,678
[Debbie] How is he?

607
00:39:07,178 --> 00:39:08,263
He's at Cedars.

608
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:12,809
The doctor said he had a bad reaction
to mixing alcohol with his medication.

609
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:16,354
The doctor just told you that?

610
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:17,647
My dad is a doctor too.

611
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:20,733
And we're his friends, Bret.

612
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:22,694
Or at least I am.

613
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:23,820
[Bret] Hmm.

614
00:39:27,907 --> 00:39:29,325
What did you say to him?

615
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:32,161
Who?

616
00:39:34,497 --> 00:39:36,749
Oh. Robert. Nothing.

617
00:39:36,833 --> 00:39:38,543
[Susan] I saw you whisper
something to him,

618
00:39:38,626 --> 00:39:41,254
and whatever you said really upset him.

619
00:39:42,005 --> 00:39:43,464
I didn't say anything to him.

620
00:39:43,548 --> 00:39:45,967
-I know who you are.
-You don't know me, man.

621
00:39:47,135 --> 00:39:49,012
I know more than you think.

622
00:39:53,182 --> 00:39:55,935
[whispers] I know you killed your mom.

623
00:40:06,446 --> 00:40:07,447
Right.

624
00:40:09,324 --> 00:40:10,867
What did he whisper to you?

625
00:40:10,950 --> 00:40:12,243
-When?
-After you kissed him.

626
00:40:12,327 --> 00:40:13,828
-That was CPR.
-Sure.

627
00:40:15,872 --> 00:40:17,749
He just said thank you.

628
00:40:22,295 --> 00:40:24,422
[♪ tense music plays]

629
00:40:32,847 --> 00:40:37,060
[Bret] It was the first time we had lied
to each other's faces and both known it.

630
00:40:38,728 --> 00:40:40,063
In that moment,

631
00:40:40,146 --> 00:40:43,942
I knew the thing I had desired
and feared most had come to pass.

632
00:40:44,776 --> 00:40:47,862
I had entered
the world of adults and death,

633
00:40:47,946 --> 00:40:50,031
and the door had closed behind me.

634
00:40:52,575 --> 00:40:54,661
I would never feel like a kid again.

635
00:40:55,870 --> 00:40:57,622
I'd never felt more grown up.

636
00:41:00,333 --> 00:41:02,168
And I'd never felt more alone.

637
00:41:24,774 --> 00:41:26,651
[♪ "Icehouse" playing]

638
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:28,236
[Susan] Look how pretty the sky is.

639
00:41:36,285 --> 00:41:40,248
Debbie, you don't wanna look at the sky?

640
00:41:41,833 --> 00:41:43,584
I've seen it already.

641
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:49,340
♪ It's always cold inside the icehouse ♪

642
00:41:53,302 --> 00:41:57,432
♪ Though the rivers never freeze ♪

643
00:42:01,394 --> 00:42:05,815
♪ There's a girl outside the icehouse… ♪

644
00:42:05,898 --> 00:42:09,360
-[person whimpering]
-[dogs barking]

645
00:42:09,444 --> 00:42:12,864
[whimpering continues]

646
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:25,793
[barking continues]

647
00:42:29,338 --> 00:42:32,467
[whimpering]

648
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:34,093
Help!

649
00:42:35,136 --> 00:42:36,137
Help!

650
00:42:37,055 --> 00:42:41,642
♪ The devil lives inside the icehouse ♪

651
00:42:45,146 --> 00:42:49,484
♪ At least that's what the old ones say ♪

652
00:42:51,611 --> 00:42:55,531
♪ They say,
"He came a long time ago" ♪

653
00:42:57,200 --> 00:43:00,536
♪ "He came here in the winter snow" ♪

654
00:43:01,829 --> 00:43:05,625
♪ Now it's colder every day ♪

655
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:13,883
♪ But she's still dreaming
Through the summer ♪

656
00:43:18,179 --> 00:43:21,724
♪ And she's hoping through the spring ♪

657
00:43:25,520 --> 00:43:30,399
♪ She says she's got no time
For winter nights ♪

658
00:43:33,069 --> 00:43:36,989
♪ She doesn't notice
As the days grow darker ♪

659
00:43:37,073 --> 00:43:40,952
♪ She can't remember getting any older ♪

660
00:43:41,994 --> 00:43:46,499
♪ There's no love inside the icehouse ♪

661
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:19,615
♪ And now she's dreaming of a new love ♪

662
00:44:22,910 --> 00:44:26,581
♪ And she hopes he'll be there soon ♪

663
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:34,797
♪ There's no love inside the icehouse ♪

